  spec's contract is now wrong). (2) Active enumeration drift — the
  spec pins "eight canonical agents" but discover surfaces nine
  (aide-explorer is on disk and registered). (3) Active post-move
  drift — see prior cycle.
intent: >
  installAgents was stamped aligned under the src/tools/init/ regime.
  Three drifts have accumulated since: the fixed-`brain`-key shift made
  every outcome that names "Obsidian MCP" / "mcpServers: [obsidian]"
  stale; the agent roster grew from eight to nine; and the post-move
  identity drift remains. The handoff explicitly names the agent
  frontmatter sweep as Remaining work — meaning the spec's contract
  currently disagrees with both the canonical doctrine and the in-flight
