## Retro

The agent rename (aide-researcher -> aide-domain-expert, aide-domain-expert -> aide-strategist) and the addition of aide-aligner and aide-auditor updated the canonical docs (.aide/docs/index.md), the actual agent files (.claude/agents/aide/), and the initContent registry, but did not propagate to the installAgents spec. An alignment check should have been run after any commit that changes the Pipeline Agents table, since every install submodule spec encodes facts from that table. The spec-writer should have called aide_discover and cross-referenced the canonical table before writing outcomes that enumerate agents by name and count.

The current (post-move) drift is positional, not enumerative — the agent
roster is correct, but the spec's `scope` and parent-framing still name
the old module identity. Same pattern as the rest of the moved subtree:
folder rename plus new consumer should have triggered a `/aide:spec` pass.
